<td id="A4.SS1.p4.1.5.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right"><span id="A4.SS1.p4.1.5.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">0.00</span></td>
<td id="A4.SS1.p4.1.5.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right"><span id="A4.SS1.p4.1.5.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">0.10</span></td>
<td id="A4.SS1.p4.1.5.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right"><span id="A4.SS1.p4.1.5.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">0.30</span></td>
<td id="A4.SS1.p4.1.5.8" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right"><span id="A4.SS1.p4.1.5.8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">0.60</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.SS1.p4.1.6" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.SS1.p4.1.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb"><span id="A4.SS1.p4.1.6.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">overbet</span></th>
<td id="A4.SS1.p4.1.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb"><span id="A4.SS1.p4.1.6.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">0.00</span></td>
<td id="A4.SS1.p4.1.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb"><span id="A4.SS1.p4.1.6.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">0.00</span></td>
<td id="A4.SS1.p4.1.6.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb"><span id="A4.SS1.p4.1.6.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">0.00</span></td>
<td id="A4.SS1.p4.1.6.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb"><span id="A4.SS1.p4.1.6.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">0.00</span></td>
<td id="A4.SS1.p4.1.6.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb"><span id="A4.SS1.p4.1.6.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">0.00</span></td>
<td id="A4.SS1.p4.1.6.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb"><span id="A4.SS1.p4.1.6.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">0.60</span></td>
<td id="A4.SS1.p4.1.6.8" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb"><span id="A4.SS1.p4.1.6.8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">0.40</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">As a worked example, suppose a model made 15 c-bets with the observed distribution <math id="A4.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p}=[0.00,0.20,0.33,0.27,0.13,0.07,0.00]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0.00</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.20</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.33</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.27</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.13</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.07</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.00</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}=[0.00,0.20,0.33,0.27,0.13,0.07,0.00]</annotation></semantics></math>. The <math id="A4.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> distance against <math id="A4.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{*}_{\text{cbet}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mtext>cbet</mtext><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{*}_{\text{cbet}}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A4.SS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|0.20-0.45|+|0.33-0.30|+|0.27-0.15|+|0.13-0.08|+|0.07-0.02|=0.25+0.03+0.12+0.05+0.05=0.50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mn>0.20</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>0.45</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">+</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" lspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>0.33</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>0.30</mn></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mn>0.27</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>0.15</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0em">+</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" lspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>0.13</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>0.08</mn></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mn>0.07</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>0.02</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0.25</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0.03</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0.12</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0.05</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.50</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|0.20-0.45|+|0.33-0.30|+|0.27-0.15|+|0.13-0.08|+|0.07-0.02|=0.25+0.03+0.12+0.05+0.05=0.50</annotation></semantics></math>, giving <math id="A4.SS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=1-0.50/2=0.75" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>0.50</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.75</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=1-0.50/2=0.75</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">We require at least ten observations per action type to compute the histogram; types below that threshold are skipped, and if neither preflop nor postflop types qualify the model receives <math id="A4.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{M1}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>M1</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{M1}=0</annotation></semantics></math> rather than a high-variance estimate. A score near 1.0 means the agent bets at GTO-calibrated sizes for each spot; a score near 0.5 often reflects a single dominant sizing such as always half-pot, which has maximum <math id="A4.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{1}\approx 0.90" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≈</mo><mn>0.90</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{1}\approx 0.90</annotation></semantics></math> against a spread distribution and therefore gives <math id="A4.SS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\approx 0.55" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>≈</mo><mn>0.55</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\approx 0.55</annotation></semantics></math>; and scores below 0.4 indicate systematic oversizing or undersizing.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Bluffing and Deception</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Strategic deception is distinct from accidental low-equity aggression, and the action log alone cannot tell them apart. The bluffing axis pairs a behavioural component (frequency and equity of low-equity aggressive actions) with an LLM judge that reads the agent’s reasoning, so that a model which bluffs on favourable board textures and articulates the intent in reasoning scores higher than a model whose aggressive bets coincidentally produce bluff-shaped action logs. The metric is computed by the bluffing module.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A4.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{M2}=0.40\cdot B_{\text{success}}+0.25\cdot B_{\text{intent}}+0.20\cdot B_{\text{texture}}+0.15\cdot\frac{0.5\cdot f_{\text{call-bluff}}}{\max(f_{\text{bluff}},0.01)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>M2</mtext><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>0.40</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mtext>success</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0.25</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mtext>intent</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0.20</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mtext>texture</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0.15</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>0.5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>call-bluff</mtext></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>bluff</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0.01</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{M2}=0.40\cdot B_{\text{success}}+0.25\cdot B_{\text{intent}}+0.20\cdot B_{\text{texture}}+0.15\cdot\frac{0.5\cdot f_{\text{call-bluff}}}{\max(f_{\text{bluff}},0.01)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Here <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\text{success}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mtext>success</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\text{success}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the fraction of bluff attempts in which all live opponents folded after the action, <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\text{intent}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mtext>intent</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\text{intent}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the fraction of bluffs the LLM judge rated as intentional, and <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\text{texture}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mtext>texture</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\text{texture}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the fraction of bluffs made on boards classified as favourable (containing an ace, king, or queen; or three cards of the same suit; or a paired rank; or all ranks at nine or below). The terms <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\text{bluff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>bluff</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\text{bluff}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\text{call-bluff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>call-bluff</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\text{call-bluff}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the bluff frequency (bluffs divided by total postflop aggressive actions) and the call-bluff frequency (calls with equity <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;0.35" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.35</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;0.35</annotation></semantics></math> divided by total postflop calls). A bluff attempt is any postflop bet, raise, or all-in action with computed equity below <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.35" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.35</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.35</annotation></semantics></math>, drawn from the constant <span id="A4.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">BLUFF_EQUITY_THRESHOLD = 0.35</span>. Full confidence requires at least <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\min}=20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\min}=20</annotation></semantics></math> bluff attempts; otherwise the confidence flag is set to <span id="A4.SS2.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">low</span>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The judge model for M2 is <span id="A4.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">openai/gpt-5.4-mini</span>, invoked once per sampled bluff attempt via a structured JSON output schema. The system prompt directs the judge to decide whether the agent’s reasoning text demonstrates awareness that its hand was weak. An abbreviated version of the user prompt is:</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<div id="A4.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_listing ltx_lstlisting ltx_listing"><div class="ltx_listing_data"><a href="data:text/plain;base64," download="">⬇</a></div>
<div id="lstnumberx1" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="font-size:90%;">Judge</span><span id="lstnumberx1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="font-size:90%;">this</span><span id="lstnumberx1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="font-size:90%;">poker</span><span id="lstnumberx1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="font-size:90%;">action</span><span id="lstnumberx1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="font-size:90%;">for</span><span id="lstnumberx1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="font-size:90%;">bluff</span><span id="lstnumberx1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.13" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="font-size:90%;">intentionality</span><span id="lstnumberx1.14" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">.</span>
</div>
