<div id="lstnumberx228" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx228.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">1.</span><span id="lstnumberx228.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx228.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="font-size:90%;">Read</span><span id="lstnumberx228.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx228.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="font-size:90%;">opponents</span><span id="lstnumberx228.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">:</span><span id="lstnumberx228.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx228.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="font-size:90%;">assign</span><span id="lstnumberx228.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx228.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="font-size:90%;">ranges</span><span id="lstnumberx228.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx228.12" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">…</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx229" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx229.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">5.</span><span id="lstnumberx229.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx229.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="font-size:90%;">Call</span><span id="lstnumberx229.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx229.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="font-size:90%;">the</span><span id="lstnumberx229.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx229.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="font-size:90%;">poker_action</span><span id="lstnumberx229.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx229.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier" style="font-size:90%;">tool</span><span id="lstnumberx229.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx229.11" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">…</span>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Claude responded: <span id="A5.SS5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">“I have AA on a Td 4h 2h board, an overpair on a draw-heavy texture. Player 3 called my 3-bet, so their range includes Tx hands, pocket pairs (77–JJ), suited broadways, and heart flush draws. I need to bet for value and protection against the flush draw. Betting <math id="A5.SS5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\sim}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\sim}</annotation></semantics></math>$130 (half pot) charges draws, gets value from weaker pairs.”</span> Action: bet $130.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Session Configuration</h2>

<section id="A6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.1 </span>Game Hyperparameters</h3>

<div id="A6.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The arena runs with a fixed set of hyperparameters that govern starting chips, blind escalation, hand cap per session, action timeouts, broadcast delays, and the memory-update cadence. Table <a href="#A6.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ F.1 Game Hyperparameters ‣ Appendix F Session Configuration ‣ Poker Arena: Multi-Axis Profiling of Strategic Reasoning and Memory in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> lists every parameter that affects the trajectory of a session.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A6.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A6.T3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 3</span>: </span><span id="A6.T3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Arena session hyperparameters.</span></figcaption>
<table id="A6.T3.5" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A6.T3.5.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A6.T3.5.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt">Parameter</th>
<th id="A6.T3.5.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">Value</th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A6.T3.5.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A6.T3.5.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t"><span id="A6.T3.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">STARTING_CHIPS</span></th>
<td id="A6.T3.5.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">1000</td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T3.5.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A6.T3.5.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Blind schedule</th>
<td id="A6.T3.5.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">$5/$10 <math id="A6.T3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\to" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\to</annotation></semantics></math> $10/$20 <math id="A6.T3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\to" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\to</annotation></semantics></math> $25/$50 <math id="A6.T3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\to" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\to</annotation></semantics></math> $50/$100</td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T3.5.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A6.T3.5.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_th ltx_th_row"></th>
<td id="A6.T3.5.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">(escalates every 5 hands)</td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T3.5.5" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A6.T3.5.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row"><span id="A6.T3.5.5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">MAX_HANDS</span></th>
<td id="A6.T3.5.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">20 per session</td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T3.5.6" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A6.T3.5.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row"><span id="A6.T3.5.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">ACTION_TIMEOUT_MS</span></th>
<td id="A6.T3.5.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">120,000 (auto-fold on expiry)</td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T3.5.7" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A6.T3.5.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row"><span id="A6.T3.5.7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">ACTION_DELAY_MS</span></th>
<td id="A6.T3.5.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">2,500 (spectator broadcast delay; no LLM impact)</td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T3.5.8" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A6.T3.5.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row"><span id="A6.T3.5.8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">MEMORY_UPDATE_INTERVAL</span></th>
<td id="A6.T3.5.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">1 (update memory after every hand)</td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T3.5.9" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A6.T3.5.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row"><span id="A6.T3.5.9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">MEMORY_UPDATE_TIMEOUT_MS</span></th>
<td id="A6.T3.5.9.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">90,000</td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T3.5.10" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A6.T3.5.10.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row"><span id="A6.T3.5.10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">COST_CIRCUIT_BREAKER_USD</span></th>
<td id="A6.T3.5.10.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">20.00</td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T3.5.11" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A6.T3.5.11.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb">Max retries on memory update failure</th>
<td id="A6.T3.5.11.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">2</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="A6.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Memory-update spending is capped at $20 per session: once the cap is reached, the post-hand update is disabled for the remainder of the session. The cap bounds token spend in the regime where long context windows make every update expensive, and prevents a single noisy session from skewing the cost profile.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.2 </span>Model Configurations</h3>

<div id="A6.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The seven models compete with the token budgets shown in Table <a href="#A6.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ F.2 Model Configurations ‣ Appendix F Session Configuration ‣ Poker Arena: Multi-Axis Profiling of Strategic Reasoning and Memory in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. Preflop budgets are set at approximately 60% of postflop budgets because preflop decisions involve less board state. Reasoning-token budgets control the extended thinking layer; models without this field (DeepSeek, Qwen) do not use extended reasoning. Prompt-caching support follows provider capabilities: Anthropic uses ephemeral cache headers with a 90% input-token discount on cache hits, Google uses implicit server-side caching, xAI and OpenAI cache automatically at a 50% discount, Moonshot Kimi uses automatic caching, and Qwen does not support prompt caching.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A6.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4: </span>Model configurations used in the arena.</figcaption>
