</table>
</figure>
<div id="A7.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">All <math id="A7.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-values exceed 0.05, so the memory advantage for Claude and Kimi (condition B higher) and the GPT disadvantage (condition A higher) are directionally consistent with the main-paper discussion but do not reach statistical significance at <math id="A7.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=10</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A7.F4" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2606.13815v1/fig4_ablation.svg" id="A7.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:262/164;" width="262" height="164"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A7.F4.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 4</span>: </span><span id="A7.F4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Mean chip delta per session under the two ablation conditions for Claude, GPT, and Kimi. Solid bars give condition A (no persistent memory, seeded from session 50); hatched bars give condition B (full persistent memory with the same seeds). Error bars span <math id="A7.F4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm 1\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>±</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm 1\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> across the ten sessions in each cell, and the numerical annotations show the within-model <math id="A7.F4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A-B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A-B</annotation></semantics></math> difference in mean chip delta.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.4 </span>Bootstrap Confidence Intervals and Rank Correlation</h3>

<div id="A7.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All statistics below were computed with <math id="A7.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=10{,}000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10,000</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=10{,}000</annotation></semantics></math> bootstrap resamples and a fixed RNG seed (<span id="A7.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">20260416</span>) for full reproducibility.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The first table gives bootstrap 95% confidence intervals on the cumulative chip delta <math id="A7.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{s=1}^{50}\Delta_{m,s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>50</mn></msubsup><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{s=1}^{50}\Delta_{m,s}</annotation></semantics></math> for each model:</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A7.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
